name: instrument-repair
kind: inferred
shape: categorical
face: in
membrane: false
note: |
  Fires when the measuring apparatus itself is made right — a checker, board,
  or map whose output was WRONG (not merely coarse) is repaired, so the numbers
  it prints change while the thing measured never moved.

  Distinct from `measurement-artifact`, which names the misread when it is
  discovered, and from `instrument-sharpened`, where the instrument was correct
  but blunt and gains discrimination it lacked. Repair is for a wrong model
  inside the instrument: the artifact signal fired at the discovery; this one
  fires when the fix lands.

  Canonical instance: js-parity-map read koru_std/ flat, registering
  part files (store.new.kz) as unimportable modules named "store.new";
  every store:*/list:* call site missed against the primary and 27.0% of
  the corpus landed DO-NOT-TRUST — a property of the map, not the corpus.
  Joining on the declared ~part lines dropped the tail to 0.3% with zero
  corpus or stdlib change (465a1a2f).
route: surface
